# Design / internal docs (kept local)
DESIGN.md
docs/
.docs/
# `.claude/` and `.agents/` hold PERSONAL settings (settings.local.json), local
# agent definitions and hooks -- none of which belong to anybody but their owner.
# Their `skills/` directories are different: the rc-repro skill is a project
# artifact, and committing it is how a fresh clone teaches an agent to drive this
# tool correctly. So the contents are ignored and that one subdirectory is not,
# which needs `dir/*` rather than `dir/` -- git will not descend into an excluded
# directory to re-include something inside it.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# Everything else under `.claude/` is one person's tooling and stays out: `agents/`,
# `hooks/`, `settings.json` and `settings.local.json`. They describe how somebody
# chooses to work on this repository, not what the repository is -- and a whitelist
# for them is a standing invitation to re-commit whatever the tool regenerates.
# `skills/` above is the exception because the rc-repro skill is a project artifact.
.codex/
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
